# skill: linked-list-static

## Contract

Static linked-list — array-based, no pointers.
- Max 64 nodes, node index 0 is reserved as NULL sentinel.
- All nodes allocated from a pre-sized array; no dynamic memory.

### Structures

```
struct LLNode {
    int data;
    int next;   // index of next node, 0 = NULL
};

struct StaticLinkedList {
    struct LLNode nodes[64];
    int free_head;  // index of first free node
    int size;       // active node count
};
```

### Functions

| Function | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `ll_init` | `void ll_init(struct StaticLinkedList* list)` | Initialize list, build free list |
| `ll_alloc_node` | `int ll_alloc_node(struct StaticLinkedList* list)` | Allocate from free list; returns index or 0 |
| `ll_free_node` | `void ll_free_node(struct StaticLinkedList* list, int idx)` | Return node to free list |
| `ll_push_front` | `void ll_push_front(struct StaticLinkedList* list, int data)` | Insert data at head |
| `ll_pop_front` | `int ll_pop_front(struct StaticLinkedList* list)` | Remove and return head data |

### Constants

- `LL_MAX_NODES = 64`
- `LL_NULL = 0` (sentinel, node index 0 is never used for data)

## Dependencies

- `array-base` — generic array utilities
- `memory-static` — no-heap memory discipline

## Prohibitions

`malloc`, `calloc`, `realloc`, `free` — this skill enforces static allocation only.

## Slots

| Slot | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `ll_init` | init | Initialize `StaticLinkedList` |
| `ll_alloc_node` | factory | Produce a node index from free list |
| `ll_free_node` | destructor | Return a node to free list |
| `ll_push_front` | mutator | Add node to list head |
| `ll_pop_front` | accessor | Remove and yield head value |

## Boundaries

- **Capacity**: 63 usable nodes (index 0 reserved)
- **Empty state**: `size == 0`, `nodes[0].next == LL_NULL`
- **Full state**: `free_head == LL_NULL`
- **No overflow check** in `ll_push_front` — caller must check `size < LL_MAX_NODES - 1`
- **No underflow check** in `ll_pop_front` — returns `0` on empty list (ambiguous with valid data `0`)
- **Thread safety**: None — caller must serialize access

## Examples

### Init

```c
struct StaticLinkedList list;
ll_init(&list);
// free_head = 1, size = 0, all nodes chained 1->2->...->63->NULL
```

### Push/Pop

```c
ll_push_front(&list, 42);
ll_push_front(&list, 99);
ll_pop_front(&list);  // returns 99
ll_pop_front(&list);  // returns 42
ll_pop_front(&list);  // returns 0 (empty)
```

### Full list

```c
// fill to capacity
for (int i = 0; i < 63; i++) ll_push_front(&list, i);
// free_head == LL_NULL, next push silently no-ops
```

[code]
```c
#define LL_MAX_NODES 64
#define LL_NULL 0

struct LLNode {
    int data;
    int next;
};

struct StaticLinkedList {
    struct LLNode nodes[LL_MAX_NODES];
    int free_head;
    int size;
};

void ll_init(struct StaticLinkedList* list) {
    list->size = 0;
    list->free_head = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i < LL_MAX_NODES - 1; i++) {
        list->nodes[i].next = i + 1;
    }
    list->nodes[LL_MAX_NODES - 1].next = LL_NULL;
    list->nodes[0].next = LL_NULL;
}

int ll_alloc_node(struct StaticLinkedList* list) {
    if (list->free_head == LL_NULL) return LL_NULL;
    int idx = list->free_head;
    list->free_head = list->nodes[idx].next;
    list->size++;
    return idx;
}

void ll_free_node(struct StaticLinkedList* list, int idx) {
    list->nodes[idx].next = list->free_head;
    list->free_head = idx;
    list->size--;
}

void ll_push_front(struct StaticLinkedList* list, int data) {
    int node = ll_alloc_node(list);
    if (node == LL_NULL) return;
    list->nodes[node].data = data;
    list->nodes[node].next = list->nodes[0].next;
    list->nodes[0].next = node;
}

int ll_pop_front(struct StaticLinkedList* list) {
    if (list->size == 0) return 0;
    int first = list->nodes[0].next;
    int data = list->nodes[first].data;
    list->nodes[0].next = list->nodes[first].next;
    ll_free_node(list, first);
    return data;
}
```
